mentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "South Dakota remains firmly in the Republican column at the presidential level. The state's partisan lean of roughly fifteen points Republican sets the starting point, and no public polls, expert ratings, or market signals offer a reason to move from it. The open nature of the race, with a term-limited president, removes any incumbency effect in either direction.\n\nWithout state-level polling, the forecast rests entirely on fundamentals, which keeps uncertainty wide. South Dakota has voted Republican by double digits in every recent presidential election, and there is no evidence of a competitive Democratic operation or unusual local dynamics. A large national swing would be needed to put the state in play, and even then it would likely remain a long shot for the Democratic ticket.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0482, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0894, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0844, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0865, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0843, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.078, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0834, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0867, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0898, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0794, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0692, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0903, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.079, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0947, "margin"